 * Purnima; Jan 29 claimed Shukla Ekadashi, Drik says Amavasya; Mar 12/13 off
 * by one vs Drik month grid). The engine was right; the table was wrong.
 * Renamed to .obsolete so vitest ignores it. See TITHI_VALIDATION_PLAN.md.
 */
/**
 * Drik Panchang Comparison Test
 *
 * Comprehensive comparison of engine tithi calculations against Drik Panchang.
 *
 * Reference: drikpanchang.com — The standard reference for Hindu panchang calculations.
 *
 * Methodology:
 * - Engine calculates tithi at sunrise (Udaya Tithi principle)
 * - Engine uses Lahiri Ayanamsa (sidereal Nirayana)
 * - Sidereal sun/moon positions from Meeus algorithms
 * - Tithi = floor((moon_sidereal - sun_sidereal) / 12)
 *
 * For each test date, we compare:
 *   1. Tithi name at sunrise — the engine's computed result
 *   2. Whether it matches Drik Panchang's Udaya Tithi
 *   3. Sunrise time (within tolerance)
 */

import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
